      {
        "id": "intro",
        "type": "nodetool.workflows.base_node.Comment",
        "data": {
          "comment": "# Remove Grain with a Median Filter\n\nDraws a checkerboard under heavy grain and removes the grain while the edges stay sharp. Every step runs in the editor process, with no file, model or key.\n\n**How it works:** \"1 Board\" and \"2 Grain\" make the noisy image in \"3 Noisy\". A rank filter sorts the pixels around each pixel and keeps one of them. Rank 4 of a 3 by 3 window and rank 12 of a 5 by 5 window are the medians. A blur would soften the edges, and a median does not.\n\n**Try this:** Set Rank on \"Median 3x3\" to 0 for a minimum filter (darker) or 8 for a maximum filter (lighter)."
        },
